{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/383264-recruiting-mage-the-awakening-anthology-of-power-play-by-post","id":383264,"title":"[Recruiting] Mage: The Awakening - Anthology of Power (Play By Post)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-27T10:16:45-08:00","id":383264,"title":"[Recruiting] Mage: The Awakening - Anthology of Power (Play By Post)","content":"<b><span style=\"font-size:28px\">M</span><span style=\"font-size:20px\">AGE THE </span><span style=\"font-size:28px\">A</span><span style=\"font-size:20px\">WAKENING<br /> A</span>NTHOLOGY OF <span style=\"font-size:20px\">P</span>OWER</b><br /> <b>Game Intro</b><br /> <br /> <b>Synopsis</b><br /> Anthology of Power is a play by post game for Mage: The Awakening. It is set in Boston and the surrounding area of Massachusetts, featuring the Consilium and its respective Cabals described in Boston Unveiled. I have written a story consisting of nine chapters, and I'll continue to write further stories which will be played upon completion. The Anthology kicks off with:<br /> <br /> <br /> <i><u>'</u></i><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><i><u>T</u></i></span><i><u>HE </u></i><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><i><u>B</u></i></span><i><u>LACK </u></i><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><i><u>P</u></i></span><i><u>YRAMID'</u></i><ul><li>Chapter One: What Words We Haven't Read</li> <li>Chapter Two: The Door to Somewhere Not</li> <li>Chapter Three: Sanctum of the Sleeping</li> <li>Chapter Four: To Thine Own Self</li> <li>Chapter Five: Eater of Eternity</li> <li>Chapter Six: The Stones Before Nothing</li> <li>Chapter Seven: It Beckons to Thee</li> <li>Chapter Eight: Like Shards of Glass</li> <li>Chapter Nine: A Third Temple Midnight</li> </ul><br /> <b>Player Recruitment</b><br /> I'm recruiting three players. This is not a &quot;first come first serve&quot; scenario. I want to insure player compatibility. I'll choose the players and characters I feel are best for the game. I'll require anyone interested to fill out the Character Template given below, complete with a Prelude written by the player. This is a writing sample that shows me your style. Effectively, think of it as an \u201cAudition Post\u201d. About 3-5 solid paragraphs will do, but if you've got more in you, then go for it. Feel free to message me with any questions you might have. I plan on being very patient about this, waiting until I have enough submissions to choose from. So take your time. Once I've chosen the Players for my game, I'll update this section to indicate as such. Until then consider it open.<br /> <br /> *Update*<br /> This game has been filled. However, if this game is your cup of tea, let me know. I may run future games that I'll need players for.<br /> <br /> <b>Character Motivations</b><br /> As the title implies, power is the driving motivation behind these stories. This could be power as a means to a noble end, as a goal unto itself, or even to serve completely immoral reasons. However, your character must always put the Cabal first. There may be some conflicts that crop up between Characters at times, but a Cabal that has no ties of loyalty or friendship can ultimately be destructive to the game.<br /> <br /> <b>Honor System Mechanics</b><br /> I don't know about you, but I like the feel of real dice in my hands. For this reason, I won't be using any digital dice rollers for this game. Everyone may roll their own dice, and trust in one another's desire for a game in which your characters' failures are just as interesting and exciting as their successes. If not more so.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">C</span>HARACTER <span style=\"font-size:20px\">T</span>EMPLATE</b></u><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <u>Player:</u> [Optional. My name is Rod.]<br /> <u>Chronicle:</u> Anthology of Power<br /> <br /> <u>Path:</u><br /> <u>Order:</u><br /> <u>Cabal:</u> [Leave blank. Players will work on this together.]<br /> <br /> <u>Virtue:</u><br /> <u>Vice:</u><br /> <u>Concept:</u> [Optional]<br /> <br /> <b><u>Advantages:</u></b><br /> Health:<br /> Willpower:<br /> Defense:<br /> Initiative:<br /> Speed:<br /> <br /> Gnosis:<br /> Wisdom:<br /> Mana:<br /> <br /> <b><u>Attributes</u> </b><br /> Intelligence:<br /> Wits:<br /> Resolve:<br /> <br /> Strength:<br /> Dexterity:<br /> Stamina:<br /> <br /> Presence:<br /> Manipulation:<br /> Composure:<br /> <br /> [Record attributes and abilities with a numeral, not a series of dots]<br /> <br /> <b><u>Skills</u></b><br /> Academics:<br /> Computer:<br /> Crafts:<br /> Investigation:<br /> Medicine:<br /> Occult:<br /> Politics:<br /> Science:<br /> <br /> Athletics:<br /> Brawl:<br /> Drive:<br /> Firearms:<br /> Larceny:<br /> Stealth:<br /> Survival:<br /> Weaponry<br /> <br /> Animal Ken:<br /> Empathy:<br /> Expression:<br /> Intimidation:<br /> Persuasion:<br /> Socialize:<br /> Streetwise:<br /> Subterfuge:<br /> <br /> [If there is a specialty, include it after the relevant numeral in parentheses]<br /> <br /> <b><u>Merits</u></b><br /> Name (Dots; Book &amp; Page Number)<br /> [Include any narrative detail here. Such as the identity of a Mentor or Contact, or where dots in Resources or Fame might come from, etc.]<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Arcana</u>: </b><br /> <br /> <b><u>Rotes</u></b><br /> Name (Arcana; Dots; Book &amp; Page Number)<br /> Name (Arcana; Dots; Book &amp; Page Number)<br /> Name (Arcana; Dots; Book &amp; Page Number)<br /> <br /> <b><u>Nimbus</u></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Character Biography</u></b><br /> [The character\u2019s history and backstory. Be sure to review 'Awakening to Life' on pg. 67 of Mage, and the 'Question and Answer' portion on pg. 70.]<br /> <br /> <b><u>Equipment</u></b><br /> [Your character has access to anything that it is reasonable for a modern person of the developed world to have. Computers, cellphones, and a wide variety of cheaper everyday items don't need to be listed. In addition your character can possess a reasonably accessible weapon, and a vehicle. You can describe both and give their traits here. Anything more expensive, uncommon, or extreme, like night vision goggles, grenades, or sniper rifles will have to be acquired through Merits and compelling justification. Also list any Magical Tools here.]<br /> <br /> <b><u>Experience</u></b><br /> Unspent: 0<br /> Spent: 0<br /> <br /> <b>-Optional Details-</b><br /> <u>Age:<br /> Gender:</u><br /> <u>Ethnicity:</u><br /> <u>Nationality:</u><br /> <u>Hair Color:<br /> Eye Color:</u><br /> <u>Sexuality:</u><br /> <u>Spirituality</u>:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> ------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> [Write your character's Prelude here.]<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">P</span>ROLOGUE: <span style=\"font-size:20px\">T</span>HE</b> <b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">T</span></b><b>RIUMVIRATE</b></u><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <i>April 13<sup>th</sup>, 1984</i><br /> <br /> I'd swear the rain was the size of golf balls. It splattered the windshield of my old Plymouth Colt as I followed the winding driveway through the hills. When I got to the gate I swore, grumbling loudly to myself as I grabbed my umbrella and waded out into the storm to unlock it. Even with the umbrella, I was soaked through by the time I got back into the gray car. &quot;I'm too sodding old for this.&quot; Needless to say, I didn't get back out to close it. The Yanks would give me a lecture about that, but right now I couldn't bring myself to care. I was running late, which was simultaneously ironic and not the least bit unusual. It was all part of an Acanthus' charm, at least that's how I always explained the perpetual lateness. Maybe I even convinced myself sometimes.<br /> <br /> The old Gothic mansion came into view, and every time I saw it I couldn't believe that I was a partial owner. The courtyard was huge, with a big fountain at the center, and a series of archways along the path to the two double doors of the mansion. I parked the Colt next to the fountain. If the sky hadn't been falling I would have taken it to the parking area with the others' cars, but I didn't want to spend any more time in the storm than necessary. Even so, I was twice as drenched before I made it inside. The Yanks were waiting for me.<br /> <br /> &quot;You're late John.&quot; He said this to me more out of habit than as an admonition. They were used to this by now. We were both in our fifties, but his shoulder length hair was still dark brown, where mine had already turned mostly gray.<br /> <br /> &quot;Well in case you haven't noticed Miles, it is a bit soggy out. Now where's the bloody coffee, I'm freezing.&quot; He nodded towards the kitchen around the corner, and throwing my sopping coat onto a chair I poured myself a hot black mug of lifegiving caffeine. I joined my old friend at the small coffee table at the entrance hall, taking a seat across from him. &quot;Where's Amelia?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Here&quot; said a tall redheaded woman in her mid forties, but who looked more like she was in her late thirties. &quot;I saw you drive up from the window. Tell me you didn't just buy that car?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;My dear, just because one has money, doesn't mean one wastes it. Also as I do understand it, the purpose is to transport an individual from one location to another. In that regard, it would seem to live up to the advertising. If you want to flaunt your wealth, get a bloody remote for the bloody front gate.&quot;<br /> <br /> Miles sat his newspaper down and looked at his watch. &quot;It's nearly time. We should prepare.&quot; The Moros was a tall, fierce looking man in far better shape than I. Everything about him screamed an air of authority.<br /> <br /> &quot;You're kidding&quot; said Amelia. &quot;You can't possibly expect us to perform the rituals in this? Besides, the ritual space will have been completely washed out.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;You know what day it is. If we don't do it now we'd have to wait three months.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;It's Friday the thirteenth. So what? There's nothing Supernal about that!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;It has symbolic signifigance. That matters for us, and you know it.&quot;<br /> <br /> Amelia sighed, but didn't argue the point any further. Silently we each retreated to our rooms to dawn our ritual attire. Mine were a set of green robes, made from thick wool, lined with blue trim. Written upon the trim was script in Old Welsh, alongside a series of Atlantean Glyphs. I gathered a small cloth sack containing powdered incense, and my silver wand.<br /> <br /> We exited out the back door, Miles in a black Russian kaftan with a long staff of bones scortched black, and Amelia draped in red Buddhist robes with a string of wooden pentacles flowing from her neck. It was a long walk in such dreadful conditions, and we arrived at the ritual site I had spent exactly one month preparing only to find Amelia's earlier point validated. It was a mess. The wicks of all thirty candles were dripping wet, and the runes, carefully drawn in chalk, had been largely washed out. For a moment I was beginning to think that perhaps Amelia had been right. Clearly this was no condition to in which to conduct such an important ritual.<br /> <br /> Then I noticed the cup.<br /> <br /> Like my wand, it was made of silver. But most importantly, it had been filled to the brim with rainwater, and I began to smile. What perfect symbolism, after all! Knowledge raining down onto the Fallen World from Supernal Arcadia above. That, coupled with the timing made things perfect, despite the setbacks. I nodded to my fellows, and they took up positions within the stone circle we had erected behind the mansion. We formed a triangle, with Miles at the point, and I began to chant. I cleared my mind of the downpour, and the resulting cold in my bones, reminding myself that Amelia would be able to heal us of any adverse effects. It took a little over three hours, but I felt the Supernal reach down, calling on the sympathy with my Watchtower. As I neared the end, I spoke out in English for the benefit of us all. &quot;We, of the Triumvirate part the clouds of time, and bear witness to the sowing of our seeds. We gaze upon what fruits they bear, for good or for ill. Let the Black Pyramid casts its shadow across history.&quot;<br /> <br /> Images began to form in the water of the silver cup. Three people, staring back at me. Our own future, as I'd intended. Wait...no. Something was wrong. Very wrong. The image was erratic, and the waters within the cup began to froth. There was a great sound welling up with that water, like moving one's finger along the rim of a glass, but growing painfully loud. And then, the glass shatters into a million tiny pieces. The sound was filling my soul, and the shattering was terribly painful. My eyes had involuntarily closed, but I forced myself to stare back into the cup. I saw that it was not us in the waters...but three others. Mages I had never seen before. That harmonic note had reached a fever pitch, like being in the eye of a Tornado. I had the sudden sensation of being blasted along, like falling into rapids. This river of sound carried me along against my will, and reality tore away around me. The rain stopped and began again, the grass around me died and was reborn. Snow fell across the land, then gave way to blooming flowers. All of this and more happened in the blink of an eye. And still I was swept away, carried beyond.<br /> <br /> I was lost to the rapids. I couldn't breath.<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","user":"Techpriest","date":". 02-03-2015, 09:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","name":"Techpriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T12:36:21-08:00","id":383431,"title":"","content":"This sounds pretty interesting, and I'm really hungry for a Mage game, so you've got this guy hooked. Few questions, though:<br /> <br /> Is this 1st edition, 2nd edition, or a house-ruled combination of both? The character template doesn't say if the Virtue and Vice are limited to the 7 Heavenly Virtues/7 Deadly Sins or not, nor does it say if we start with 7 or 10 Merits dots. Although the lack of an Aspirations and Breaking Points section does suggest 1st edition, I just wanna make sure.<br /> <br /> Also, considering this chronicle is heavily based on the material of Boston Unveiled, I'll fetch me a copy to read as soon as possible. Are there any particular suggestions on where to start? I mean, I'll read up on everything eventually, including the appendix in the corebook, but for the sake of making a character I wanna read up on the most relevant things for that first.<br /> <br /> Once I know that, I'll start brewing up a character!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T12:47:57-08:00","id":383458,"title":"","content":"This game does not use anything from God Machine. It uses the original rules of New World of Darkness and Mage: The Awakening.<br /> <br /> While the setting itself makes use of Boston Unveiled, the first story I've written does not deal heavily with the Consilium. There is nothing about the game that would require you to read Boston Unveiled, or even the Appendix, since its largely a source material for Storytellers. Now, you're welcome to use characters from the source material as part of your character's background. They can be mentors, contacts, and so on. All of this is entirely up to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","name":"Techpriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T11:41:00-08:00","id":384375,"title":"","content":"Ok, I'm pretty interested! I'm going to make a character and post as soon as I can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","name":"Mahasamatman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2347_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T13:24:33-08:00","id":384467,"title":"","content":"Great, looking forward to seeing it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","name":"Techpriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T15:04:57-08:00","id":384527,"title":"","content":"IRRELEVANT<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <u>Player:</u> Mahasamatman<br /> <u>Chronicle:</u> Anthology of Power<br /> <br /> <u>Path:</u> Mastigos<br /> <u>Order:</u> Silver Ladder<br /> <u>Cabal:</u><br /> <u>Legacy:</u> Sisterhood of the Blessed<br /> <br /> <u>Virtue:</u> Justice<br /> <u>Vice:</u> Greed<br /> <u>Concept:</u> Charismatic operative<br /> <br /> <b><u>Advantages:</u></b><br /> Health: 7<br /> Willpower: 6<br /> Defense: 3<br /> Initiative: 6<br /> Speed: 10<br /> <br /> Gnosis: 3<br /> Wisdom: 5<br /> Mana: 12<br /> <br /> <b><u>Attributes</u> </b><br /> Intelligence: 1<br /> Wits: 3<br /> Resolve: 3<br /> <br /> Strength: 2<br /> Dexterity: 3<br /> Stamina: 2<br /> <br /> Presence: 2<br /> Manipulation: 3<br /> Composure: 3<br /> <br /> <b><u>Skills</u></b><br /> Academics: 1 (Law)<br /> Computer:<br /> Crafts:<br /> Investigation: 1<br /> Medicine:<br /> Occult: 2 (Magic)<br /> Politics:<br /> Science:<br /> <br /> Athletics: 1<br /> Brawl:<br /> Drive:<br /> Firearms: 2 (Pistol)<br /> Larceny: 1<br /> Stealth: 3<br /> Survival:<br /> Weaponry:<br /> <br /> Animal Ken:<br /> Empathy: 1<br /> Expression: 2<br /> Intimidation: 2<br /> Persuasion: 2<br /> Socialize: 2<br /> Streetwise:<br /> Subterfuge: 3<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Merits</u></b><br /> High Speech (1; Core p.84)<br /> Hallow (1; Core p.84) - probably communal with other players.<br /> Status (1; Private Investigator; WoD Core p.116)<br /> Extemporaneous Affinity (3; Banishers p.41)<br /> Mentor (1; Patrick Stein; WoD Core p.115)<br /> Satus (1; Silver Ladder; Core p.88)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Arcana</u>: </b> Mind 3, Fate 2, Space 1<br /> <br /> <b><u>Rotes</u></b><br /> Spatial Map (Space; 1; Core p.233)<br /> Powerful Recollection (Mind; 2; Free Council p.200)<br /> Glorious Shield (Mind; 3; Silver Ladder p.200)<br /> <br /> <b><u>Nimbus</u></b><br /> Fer's nimbus follows closely to his name. Fer's eyes take iron glint, burning with unbendable will. The world around seems like a perfect mechanism for a moment, every thing in its place and every man doing exactly what he needs to do. The air takes on a metalic taste, and hard choices seem easier to follow through.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Character Biography</u></b><br /> Sam Carter was born and raised in Boston. His father, Igor, is a fairly successful layer. His mother, Elizabeth, is an accountant. Sam was raised in good conditions, and given good education. However, he's about as sharp as a hammer, so Sam never managed to get good grades and become a real lawyer himself. With whatever law knowledge he got from the university, Sam went to the proffession playing to his strengths - perceptiveness and charm. Sam became a private investigator (disappointing his parents), and has been running a small office in Boston for almost 5 years now. The job doesn't give him much wealth, and Sam can barely support the lifestyle he's used to. Four years ago Sam Awakened. His life, previously a meaningless drift from day to day, now had focus. He has seen the Tower of Iron, and he has felt the iron gauntlet on his hand. Sam plunged head first into research and training. He secluded himself from the world for months, searching the limits of his abilities, honing the newfound power over mind and probability. Two years ago he was introduced into the mage society, by his future mentor, and a member of Sisterhood of the Blessed, Patrick Stein. Since then Sam has completed his formal education in the Silver Ladder taking on the shadow name &quot;Fer&quot;, and is ready to face the world once again, now with determination guiding him to power.<br /> <i>Personality and appearance:</i> Sam is somewhat selfish, but loyal. He prefers to solve problems in a peaceful way, through diplomacy and trickery, if possible. Sam places his covenant over his legacy, and his legacy over the order. Sam usually wears black and white three piece suit with a designer trench coat over it. He almost always wears his mirrorshades, as they are his Mastigos tool - a modern substitute for a mirror.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Equipment</u></b><br /> [I'll add general stuff later. Probably a phone, gun, <a href=\"http://garrisonbespoke.com/custom-suits/bulletproof-suit/\" target=\"_blank\">bulletproof suit</a>]<br /> <i>Magical Tools:</i> Path tool - mirrorshades with iron rims. Order tools - private detective id.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Experience</u></b><br /> Unspent: 0<br /> Spent: 0<br /> <br /> <b>-Optional Details-</b><br /> <u>Age: </u> 26<br /> <u>Gender:</u> Male<br /> <u>Ethnicity:</u> American<br /> <u>Nationality:</u> American<br /> <u>Hair Color: </u> Black<br /> <u>Eye Color:</u> Blue<br /> <u>Sexuality:</u> Heterosexual<br /> <u>Spirituality</u>: Atheist<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> ------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Prelude</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Three times Sam Carter dreamed of the unshakeable tower, and three times was he snatched away while still he paused on the high cliff above it. All iron and glory, it stood against the rending wind as if determined not to play by the world's rules. Mystery hung about it as clouds about a fabulous unvisited mountain; and as Sam stood breathless and expectant on that cliff, he felt his own weakness sharply. He was a tumbleweed in that wind, not the tower. He had neither goal nor determination. And as always, Sam stepped on the ladder leading to the tower, and was torn by the wind.<br /> <br /> The clock rang at 7, as it did every day, and Sam </span></span>grudgingly got out of bed, as he did every day. The morning routine flowed slowly- shaving, coffee, breakfast. It was when Sam went outside to pick up the mail that things got weird. Or rather, when Sam tried to go outside. The front door of his appartment (which doubled as his office) was impossible to open. There was no handle, the locks lost their buttons, and thick metal bars hugged the door tightly. Sam ran to the windows, but they were boarded shut, with no visible way to open them. Sam dashed to the phone, but every number he tried no longer existed. He banged on the door until his hands began to bleed, but there was no answer. Panicking, Sam sat down tried to calm himself. Clearly he was still sleeping, this couldn't possibly be true! You can't invade someone's room and change all locks, weld the door and bar the windows completely silently! This is impossible! But, no matter how hard Sam tried to wake up, nothing changed.<br /> <br /> Time seemed to drag on on, and nothing changed. Sam got hungry and ate his lunch. He tried to scream for help, or kick the door, but no one answered. Sam ate and slept without dreems. It seemed like time has stopped. No one was comming to help him. Sam was all alone in his room, with nothing to do but think. As days went by, Sam wasn't even sure if there's any point in levaing his room at all. He didn't do much with his life anyway, right? The job was pointless, the education was pointless. Why do anything? Why go anywhere? Life has no meaning, so he might as well sit in the room, right?<br /> <br /> Days went by, and as Sam pondered his life (what else was there to do?) he saw that he was wrong. Private Investigation didn't pay well, but it was fun. Sam may have been a fuck up in the university, but he made friends and learned things. If he never left the room, then it's like he doesn't exist, right? Sam couldn't allow that. He is here! He exists! He needs to leave the room and be part of the world! He needs to dream and see the Tower! As Sam focused on himself, on his identity and dreams, he felt iron on his hand. He knew what he has to do. The door shattered as the iron gauntlet struck it. For the first time in ages Sam went outside, filled with purpose. He stood upon the wide granite cliff, and the Iron Tower stood before him. Sam descended the seventy steps to it, and though the deadly wind of Pandemonium shred his flesh and broke his bones, it couldn't stop him. Sam walked into the Tower and signed his name in blood, claiming his right over reality and self.<br /> <br /> The clock rang at 7, as it did every day...<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2347,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","user":"Mahasamatman","date":".  Remade the character, see below 01-29-2015, 03:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","name":"Mahasamatman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2347_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T16:42:20-08:00","id":384599,"title":"","content":"Okay Mahasamatman, this is mostly solid, but with three problems:<br /> <br /> 1. You'll need to trade either Fate or Prime for Space. In the Mage Quick Reference on Page. 69 of Mage: The Awakening, it explains that <b>two </b>of your starting Arcana must be your Path's Ruling Arcana. If you choose to replace Prime, it also means you'll have to change your Prime Rote to a Space Rote.<br /> <br /> 2. Your Gnosis should be 1 since you haven't spent any of your Merit Dots to increase it. This also means that you can't have a Legacy, since you must be Gnosis 3.<br /> <br /> 3. On Page 39 of Banishers, it explains that the Merits listed in this supplement are impossible to learn for the other Mages. So you'll need to replace Extemporaneous Affinity.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","name":"Techpriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T16:48:32-08:00","id":384601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Techpriest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/383264-recruiting-mage-the-awakening-anthology-of-power-play-by-post?p=384599#post384599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay Mahasamatman, this is mostly solid, but with three problems:<br /> <br /> 1. You'll need to trade either Fate or Prime for Space. In the Mage Quick Reference on Page. 69 of Mage: The Awakening, it explains that <b>two </b>of your starting Arcana must be your Path's Ruling Arcana. If you choose to replace Prime, it also means you'll have to change your Prime Rote to a Space Rote.<br /> <br /> 2. Your Gnosis should be 1 since you haven't spent any of your Merit Dots to increase it. This also means that you can't have a Legacy, since you must be Gnosis 3.<br /> <br /> 3. On Page 39 of Banishers, it explains that the Merits listed in this supplement are impossible to learn for the other Mages. So you'll need to replace Extemporaneous Affinity.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Okay, I'll replace Prime for Space and the rote..<br /> 2. I did spend merit dots to increase it. I reduced Wisdom to 5 for 10xp, which is what I've spent on merits (other than the 1 dot I have left).<br /> 3. Extemporaneous Affinity just has &quot;Awakened&quot; as a prerequisite, unlike most other merits in there, and the text heavily implies that non-banishers can have it.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This Merit is intended to represent a character who has been using magic for a decent length of time without much in the way of formal magical education. Banishers who prefer to burn books rather than read them are also likely candidates for this Merit. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","name":"Mahasamatman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2347_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T17:03:19-08:00","id":384608,"title":"","content":"If you spent your 10 Experience on Merits, then your Attributes no longer make sense. I assumed you spent that 10 XP to bring your Manipulation from 3 to 4. If you didn't, then you've applied six dots in Social Attributes, when you should only have 5.<br /> <br /> Page 39 of Banishers: \u201cThese Merits represent an intuitive approach to magic practice by many (but not all) Banishers. In effect, these Merits are integral to that character's supernatural template. Therefore they're impossible for other mages (or even Banishers who didn't develop these Merits while Awakening) to learn unless the Storyteller decides otherwise.\u201d<br /> <br /> I realize the Extemporaneous Affinity Merit doesn't add the (Banisher or Storyteller's permission) part to its Prerequisites, but I believe that is an oversight, as either way the statement above applies this to all the listed Merits. This increased ability with Improvised Magic is intended to balance out the Banisher's lack of Rotes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","name":"Techpriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T17:15:55-08:00","id":384633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Techpriest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/383264-recruiting-mage-the-awakening-anthology-of-power-play-by-post?p=384608#post384608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you spent your 10 Experience on Merits, then your Attributes no longer make sense. I assumed you spent that 10 XP to bring your Manipulation from 3 to 4. If you didn't, then you've applied six dots in Social Attributes, when you should only have 5.<br /> <br /> Page 39 of Banishers: \u201cThese Merits represent an intuitive approach to magic practice by many (but not all) Banishers. In effect, these Merits are integral to that character's supernatural template. Therefore they're impossible for other mages (or even Banishers who didn't develop these Merits while Awakening) to learn unless the Storyteller decides otherwise.\u201d<br /> <br /> I realize the Extemporaneous Affinity Merit doesn't add the (Banisher or Storyteller's permission) part to its Prerequisites, but I believe that is an oversight, as either way the statement above applies this to all the listed Merits. This increased ability with Improvised Magic is intended to balance out the Banisher's lack of Rotes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Manipulation 4 was a mistake. I reduced it to 3.<br /> <br /> Okay, I'll take some other merits, although there is another merit in that book that allow non-banishers to take them - Rote Specialty (Awakened; not a full member of any order).<br /> I believe that part you are quoting doesn't refer to all listed merits. Full quote is:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Some of the following can be purchased only with the 10 bonus Merit dots that baseline Banisher characters begin with.</b> These Merits represent an intuitive approach to magic practiced by many (but not all) Banishers. In effect, these Merits are integral to that character\u2019s supernatural template. Therefore, they\u2019re impossible for other mages (or even Banishers who didn\u2019t develop these Merits while Awakening) to learn unless the Storyteller decides otherwise. </div> </div> </div>And most (but not all) merits that are &quot;banisher or permission&quot; have &quot;must be purchased with bonus Merit dots at character creation&quot; text with them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","name":"Mahasamatman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2347_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T17:19:25-08:00","id":384634,"title":"","content":"Thanks for graciously accepting my interpretation, even if you don't agree with it<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","name":"Techpriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T17:57:28-08:00","id":384657,"title":"","content":"Question. How do you treat Legacies that give you arcana that is already your Superior? Do you give the legacy's secondary arcana? I haven't looked at nMage for a while, and I'm now teeming with ideas <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","name":"Mahasamatman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2347_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T20:24:31-08:00","id":384730,"title":"","content":"Also, regarding the Merits, you have more than your 10xp would allow. If you put your remaining starting Merit Dot in, say, Hallow, then Status 1, Status 1, Mentor 1, and Extemporaneous Affinity 1 would collectively cost 8xp. Extemporaneous Affinity 3 would require an additional 10xp (4 for 2 Dots, 6 for 3 Dots), since Merits have to be bought successively.<br /> <br /> Regarding legacies, as far as I can see from the Core, you only gain the effective Ruling Arcanum benefit from the Legacy's primary Arcanum. So if you already have that Arcanum as part of your Ruling Arcana, it has no additional effect. That being said Legacies are one of the few aspects of Mage that I haven't explored much beyond the Core, so if you find something in a supplement that contradicts this, let me know and give me the Page number.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","name":"Techpriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T05:48:34-08:00","id":384921,"title":"","content":"That's what I get for making characters at 2am","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","name":"Mahasamatman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2347_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T12:08:00-08:00","id":385437,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Sam Carter (Fer)</b></u><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"https://gamesthatrocked.files.wordpress.com/2014/03/pathologic-the-bachelor.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <u>Player:</u> Mahasamatman<br /> <u>Chronicle:</u> Anthology of Power<br /> <br /> <u>Path:</u> Thyrsus<br /> <u>Order:</u> Silver Ladder<br /> <u>Cabal:</u><br /> <u>Legacy:</u> Bene Ashmedai (Silver Ladder, p.156)<br /> <br /> <u>Virtue:</u> Justice<br /> <u>Vice:</u> Lust<br /> <u>Concept:</u> Master of self<br /> <br /> <b><u>Advantages:</u></b><br /> Health: 7<br /> Willpower: 5<br /> Defense: 3<br /> Initiative: 6<br /> Speed: 10<br /> <br /> Gnosis: 3<br /> Wisdom: 5<br /> Mana: 12<br /> <br /> <b><u>Attributes</u> </b><br /> Intelligence: 1<br /> Wits: 4<br /> Resolve: 2<br /> <br /> Strength: 2<br /> Dexterity: 3<br /> Stamina: 2<br /> <br /> Presence: 2<br /> Manipulation: 3<br /> Composure: 3<br /> <br /> <b><u>Skills</u></b><br /> Academics: 1<br /> Computer:<br /> Crafts:<br /> Investigation: 1<br /> Medicine:<br /> Occult: 2 (Magic)<br /> Politics:<br /> Science:<br /> <br /> Athletics: 1<br /> Brawl:<br /> Drive:<br /> Firearms: 2 (Pistol)<br /> Larceny: 1<br /> Stealth: 3<br /> Survival:<br /> Weaponry:<br /> <br /> Animal Ken:<br /> Empathy: 1 (Lies)<br /> Expression: 2<br /> Intimidation: 2<br /> Persuasion: 4<br /> Socialize: 2<br /> Streetwise:<br /> Subterfuge: 2<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Merits</u></b><br /> High Speech (1; Core p.84)<br /> Hallow (1; Core p.84) - probably communal with other players.<br /> Status (1; Police; WoD Core p.116)<br /> Mentor (1; Patrick Stein (Foxhound); WoD Core p.115)<br /> Satus (1; Silver Ladder; Core p.88)<br /> Meditative Mind (1; WoD core p.109)<br /> Atlantean Hesychia (1; Secrets of the Ruined Temple p.111)<br /> <br /> <b><u>Flaw:</u></b> Nightmares (Summoners, p. 219)<br /> <br /> <b><u>Arcana</u>: </b>Mind 3, Spirit 2, Life 1<br /> <br /> <b><u>Rotes</u></b><br /> Helping Hand (Spirit; 1; Core p.245)<br /> Powerful Recollection (Mind; 2; Mysterium p.200)<br /> Glorious Shield (Mind; 3; Silver Ladder p.200)<br /> <br /> <b><u>Nimbus</u></b><br /> Fer's eyes take iron glint, burning with unbendable will. The world around seems like a perfect mechanism for a moment, every thing in its place and every man doing exactly what he needs to do. The air takes on a metalic taste, and hard choices seem easier to follow through.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Character Biography</u></b><br /> Sam Carter was born and raised in Boston. His father, Igor, is a fairly successful layer. His mother, Elizabeth, is an accountant. Sam was raised in good conditions, and given good education. However, he's about as sharp as a hammer, so Sam never managed to get good grades and become a real lawyer himself. With whatever law knowledge he got from the university, Sam went to the proffession playing to his strengths - perceptiveness and charm. Sam became a detective (disappointing his parents), and has been working for Boston PD for almost 5 years now. The job doesn't give him much wealth, and Sam can barely support the lifestyle he's used to. Four years ago Sam Awakened. His life, previously a meaningless drift from day to day, now had focus. He has seen the Tower of Stone, and saw the world as it truly is. Sam plunged head first into research and training. He secluded himself from the world for months, searching the limits of his abilities, honing the newfound power over mind and probability. Two years ago he was introduced into the mage society, by his future mentor, and a member of Bene Ashmedai, Patrick Stein (aka Foxhound). Since then Sam has completed his formal education in the Silver Ladder taking on the shadow name &quot;Fer&quot;, and is ready to face the world once again, now with determination guiding him to power.<br /> <br /> <i>Personality and appearance:</i> Sam is somewhat selfish, but loyal. He prefers to solve problems in a peaceful way, through diplomacy and trickery, if possible. Sam places his covenant over his legacy, and his legacy over the order. Sam usually wears red and black and has a liking for designer trench coats. He almost always wears his mirrorshades, as they are his magical tool - a modern substitute for a mirror.<br /> <br /> <i>Goals:</i> Currently Sam is working on climbing the career ladder in the police department, subtly influencing it to improve the efficiency. He rouses spirits in equipment, calms down overly agitated people with Mind magic, and stimulates minds. Sam's magical research is mostly introspective, and devoted to Goetia. Sam seeks mastery of his own flaws, and looks for grimoires and artefacts left by others who walked this path before.<br /> <br /> <i>Morning routine: </i>Each morning Sam carefuly grooms himself, performing his oblation. Before going to work Sam visits the Hallow to cast Glorious Shield (day) and Mental Shield (day). Because of this, Sam usually has to get up quite early<br /> <br /> <b><u>Equipment</u></b><br /> Sam has Glock 17 (Armory, p.65/67) as his police duty firearm, and a silenced Para-Ordnance 14-45 LDA (Armory, p.65/67) as his personal weapon. He also has a telescopic baton (Armory, p.29/30). Sam has his police bulletproof vest (Armory, p.175) and his casual suit is reinforced (mage's life is dangerous) (Armory, p.178). When on magical business Sam also carries lockpicks.<br /> Sam drives a motorcycle, gifted to him by his parents for the colledge graduation, though the vehicle now shows obvious signs of wear, since Sam doesn't maintain it properly.<br /> <br /> <i>Magical Tools:</i> Path tool - mirrorshades with copper rims. Order tools - police badge.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Experience</u></b><br /> Unspent: 0<br /> Spent: 10<br /> <br /> <b>-Optional Details-</b><br /> <u>Age: </u>26<br /> <u>Gender:</u> Male<br /> <u>Ethnicity:</u> American<br /> <u>Nationality:</u> American<br /> <u>Hair Color: </u>Black<br /> <u>Eye Color:</u> Blue<br /> <u>Sexuality:</u> Heterosexual<br /> <u>Spirituality</u>: Atheist<br /> <br /> <br /> ------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Prelude</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Three times Sam Carter dreamed of the unshakeable tower, and three times was he snatched away while still he paused on the high cliff above it. All copper and glory, it stood against the rending wind as if determined not to play by the world's rules. Mystery hung about it as clouds about a fabulous unvisited mountain; and as Sam stood breathless and expectant on that cliff, he felt his own weakness sharply. He was a tumbleweed in that wind, not the tower. He had neither goal nor determination. And as always, Sam stepped on the ladder leading to the tower, and was torn by the wind.<br /> <br /> The clock rang at 7, as it did every day, and Sam </span></span>grudgingly got out of bed, as he did every day. The morning routine flowed slowly- shaving, coffee, breakfast. It was when Sam went outside to pick up the mail that things got weird. Or rather, when Sam tried to go outside. The front door of his appartment was impossible to open. There was no handle, the locks lost their buttons, and thick metal bars hugged the door tightly. Sam ran to the windows, but they were boarded shut, with no visible way to open them. Sam dashed to the phone, but every number he tried no longer existed. He banged on the door until his hands began to bleed, but there was no answer. Panicking, Sam sat down tried to calm himself. Clearly he was still sleeping, this couldn't possibly be true! You can't invade someone's room and change all locks, weld the door and bar the windows completely silently! This is impossible! But, no matter how hard Sam tried to wake up, nothing changed.<br /> <br /> Time seemed to drag on on, and nothing changed. Sam got hungry and ate his lunch. He tried to scream for help, or kick the door, but no one answered. Sam ate and slept without dreems. It seemed like time has stopped. No one was comming to help him. Sam was all alone in his room, with nothing to do but think. As days went by, Sam wasn't even sure if there's any point in levaing his room at all. He didn't do much with his life anyway, right? The job was pointless, the education was pointless. Why do anything? Why go anywhere? Life has no meaning, so he might as well sit in the room, right?<br /> <br /> Days went by, and as Sam pondered his life (what else was there to do?) he saw that he was wrong. Police work didn't pay very well, but it was fun. Sam may have been a fuck up in the university, but he made friends and learned things. If he never left the room, then it's like he doesn't exist, right? Sam couldn't allow that. He is here! He exists! He needs to leave the room and be part of the world! He needs to dream and see the Tower! As Sam focused on himself, on his identity and dreams, he felt things change. He knew what he has to do. The door shattered as Sam's hand struck it. For the first time in ages Sam went outside, filled with purpose. He stood upon the wide granite cliff, and the Stone Watchtower stood before him. Sam descended the seventy steps to it, and though the deadly wind shred his flesh and broke his bones, it couldn't stop him. Sam walked into the Tower and signed his name in blood, claiming his right over reality and self. He felt the world around him change. Where once there was a barren waste now were lush gardens. Where deadly wind once tore everything now ran wild beasts and spirits. <i>The world had purpose.</i><br /> <br /> The clock rang at 7, as it did every day...<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2347,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","user":"Mahasamatman","date":". 02-01-2015, 07:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","name":"Mahasamatman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2347_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T13:06:21-08:00","id":386618,"title":"","content":"<br /> <u>Player:</u> Kenneth<br /> <u>Chronicle:</u> Anthology of Power<br /> <br /> <u>Path:</u> Mastigos<br /> <u>Order:</u> Free Council<br /> <u>Cabal:</u> [Leave blank. Players will work on this together.]<br /> <br /> <u>Virtue:</u> Hope<br /> <u>Vice:</u> Pride<br /> <u>Concept:</u> Beleagured Scientist<br /> <br /> <b><u>Advantages:</u></b><br /> Health: 7<br /> Willpower: 6<br /> Defense: 2<br /> Initiative: 5<br /> Speed: 9<br /> <br /> Gnosis: 3<br /> Wisdom: 5<br /> Mana: 12/12<br /> <br /> <b><u>Attributes</u> </b><br /> Intelligence: 4<br /> Wits: 3 (I'm aware that technically the math here is wrong, but otherwise I'd be moving the dot to Resolve or Intelligence and buying Wits to 2 with a 5 in Intelligence or a 4 in Resolve. Which, while more cost efficient for me, seems more game breaking than just popping it into Wits.)<br /> Resolve: 3 &lt;-- 2+Mastigos bonus of 1 to Resolve<br /> <br /> Strength: 2<br /> Dexterity: 2<br /> Stamina: 2<br /> <br /> Presence: 2<br /> Manipulation: 2<br /> Composure: 3<br /> <br /> [Record attributes and abilities with a numeral, not a series of dots]<br /> <br /> <b><u>Skills</u></b><br /> Academics: 1<br /> Computer: 4<br /> Crafts:<br /> Investigation: +<br /> Medicine: 3 diseases<br /> Occult:<br /> Politics:<br /> Science: 4 machinery<br /> <br /> Athletics:<br /> Brawl:<br /> Drive: 1<br /> Firearms: 2<br /> Larceny:1<br /> Stealth:<br /> Survival:<br /> Weaponry:<br /> <br /> Animal Ken:<br /> Empathy: 3<br /> Expression:<br /> Intimidation:<br /> Persuasion: 2 (logical arguments)<br /> Socialize: 1<br /> Streetwise: 1<br /> Subterfuge:<br /> <br /> [If there is a specialty, include it after the relevant numeral in parentheses]<br /> <br /> <b><u>Merits</u></b><br /> Name (Dots; Book &amp; Page Number)<br /> [Include any narrative detail here. Such as the identity of a Mentor or Contact, or where dots in Resources or Fame might come from, etc.]<br /> Resources 1 (Don't know the page off the top of my head, but I'm sure you know what it does) He had spent pretty much every dime he had from his research grants on finding a cure for his son's *insert disease here*.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Arcana</u>: </b><br /> Life 3<br /> Mind 2<br /> Space 1<br /> <b><u>Rotes<br /> (</u>Still need to pick specific rotes, but they'll basically be 1 to heal sicknesses, 1 to heal in general and 1 to attack with the machines)</b><br /> Name (Arcana; Dots; Book &amp; Page Number)<br /> Name (Arcana; Dots; Book &amp; Page Number)<br /> Name (Arcana; Dots; Book &amp; Page Number)<br /> <br /> <b><u>Nimbus</u></b><br /> I don't recall what a nimbus actually is, I'm more accustomed to oMage, but I'll look it up and fill it in before we start.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Character Biography</u></b><br /> Still need to pick a name (usually the hardest part for me) but I can give a brief backstory for you to consider. He rather grew up in a rather wealthy Bostonian family and was very well educated (Would have loved to put a couple more points into Academics to represent that. Sadly, I needed the others where I placed them) After getting a doctorate in biotechnology he eventually settled down with his wife (name) and had the first of two children (name) who was diagnosed with a previously unknown disease with no available methods to treat it. Around this time, their second child (name) was born and blessedly didn't share his brother's condition. Even with this bout of fortune, they had to spend the majority of their fortune just trying to keep (son 1) alive while a cure was being researched. Unfortunately, no cure was found and they had finally run out of money and time. It was then that the Awakening occured and (char name) was able to make the life saving medical breakthrough to save his son's life. Despite this, many of their supposed friends abandoned them after they lost their fortune and they're still struggling to recover their former lifestyle.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Equipment</u></b><br /> [Your character has access to anything that it is reasonable for a modern person of the developed world to have. Computers, cellphones, and a wide variety of cheaper everyday items don't need to be listed. In addition your character can possess a reasonably accessible weapon, and a vehicle. You can describe both and give their traits here. Anything more expensive, uncommon, or extreme, like night vision goggles, grenades, or sniper rifles will have to be acquired through Merits and compelling justification. Also list any Magical Tools here.]<br /> Mostly just his Foci which are billions self replicating nanomachines responding to a relay in his head and the other things mentioned above like computer and cell phone.<br /> <b><u>Experience</u></b><br /> Unspent: 0<br /> Spent: 0<br /> <br /> <b>-Optional Details-</b><br /> <u>Age: 35<br /> Gender: M</u><br /> <u>Ethnicity: C</u><br /> <u>Nationality: US</u><br /> <u>Hair Color: Black<br /> Eye Color: Green</u><br /> <u>Sexuality: Hetero</u><br /> <u>Spirituality</u>: Formerly atheist, now agnostic.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> ------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> [Write your character's Prelude here.]<br /> <br /> This really depends what kind of story you want to tell. Already included his Awakening and such in the biography","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4017,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4017-angryicecream","user":"angryicecream","date":". 01-30-2015, 04:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4017-angryicecream","name":"angryicecream","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T17:25:00-08:00","id":386870,"title":"","content":"I've added a Prologue to the opening post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","name":"Techpriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T23:52:35-08:00","id":387127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Techpriest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/383264-recruiting-mage-the-awakening-anthology-of-power-play-by-post?p=386870#post386870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've added a Prologue to the opening post.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess they've created...<br /> <b>(\u2022_\u2022)<br /> ( \u2022_\u2022)&gt;\u2310\u25a0-\u25a0<br /> (\u2310\u25a0_\u25a0)</b><br /> A Time Paradox!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","name":"Mahasamatman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2347_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T15:18:09-08:00","id":387670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahasamatman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/383264-recruiting-mage-the-awakening-anthology-of-power-play-by-post?p=387127#post387127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess they've created...<br /> <b>(\u2022_\u2022)<br /> ( \u2022_\u2022)&gt;\u2310\u25a0-\u25a0<br /> (\u2310\u25a0_\u25a0)</b><br /> A Time Paradox!</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6YMPAH67f4o\" target=\"_blank\">YEEEEEEEEEEEAH!</a><br /> <br /> Have a beatstick, everybody! I've played lots of mental/social-based characters as of late, so I wanted a good ol' combat-based character for a nice change of pace.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <u>Player:</u> Epicarp (or crapcarp, whichever you prefer)<br /> <u>Chronicle:</u> Anthology of Power<br /> <br /> <u>Shadow Name:</u> Phoenix<br /> <u>Sleeper Name:</u> Garrick Royce (this is not his real name, that's below. Rather, this is the name he uses when among Sleepers or other supernaturals)<br /> <u>Real Name:</u> Kemp Walt Dexter<br /> <br /> <u>Path:</u> Obrimos<br /> <u>Order:</u> Adamantine Arrow<br /> <u>Cabal:</u><br /> <u>Legacy:</u> (Tamer of Fire; Legacies: the Ancient p. 39)<br /> <br /> <u>Virtue:</u> Faith<br /> <u>Vice:</u> Wrath<br /> <u>Concept:</u> Hero in a World of Darkness<br /> <br /> <b><u>Advantages:</u></b><br /> Health: 7<br /> Willpower: 5<br /> Defense: 2<br /> Initiative: 4<br /> Speed: 11<br /> Size: 5<br /> <br /> Gnosis: 3<br /> Wisdom: 5<br /> Mana: 5/12<br /> <br /> <b><u>Attributes</u> </b><br /> Intelligence: 2<br /> Wits: 3<br /> Resolve: 3<br /> <br /> Strength: 4<br /> Dexterity: 2<br /> Stamina: 2<br /> <br /> Presence: 3<br /> Manipulation: 1<br /> Composure: 2<br /> <br /> <b><u>Skills</u></b><br /> Academics:<br /> Computer:<br /> Crafts:<br /> Investigation:<br /> Medicine: 2<br /> Occult: 2 (Mythology)<br /> Politics:<br /> Science:<br /> <br /> Athletics: 3<br /> Brawl: 4 (Muay Thai)<br /> Drive:<br /> Firearms:<br /> Larceny:<br /> Stealth:<br /> Survival:<br /> Weaponry: 4 (Polearms)<br /> <br /> Animal Ken:<br /> Empathy: 2<br /> Expression: 3<br /> Intimidation: 2<br /> Persuasion:<br /> Socialize:<br /> Streetwise:<br /> Subterfuge:<br /> <br /> <b><u>Merits</u></b><br /> <br /> Muay Thai - Aggressive Striking (2; WoD p. 110, Armory Reloaded p. 65 &amp; 110)<br /> Staff Fighting (1; Armory p. 213)<br /> Status - Adamantine Arrow (1; Core p. 88)<br /> High Speech (1; Core p. 84)<br /> Status - Dojo (1; WoD p. 116)<br /> <br /> He works at a local dojo that has some good weapons. Among other things, this allows him to borrow some of these weapons so long as he can justify it in some way. I'll let the ST decide on the specifics of the weapons and what's needed to convince his employer to borrow them.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Arcana</u>:</b> Forces 2, Mind 2, Prime 1, Life 1<br /> <br /> <b><u>Rotes</u></b><br /> <br /> Kinetic Blow (Forces; 2; Strength + Brawl or Weaponry + Forces; Core p. 166)<br /> Sense Consciousness (Mind; 1; Wits + Empathy + Mind; Core p. 206)<br /> Mental Shield (Mind; 2; Resolve + Occult + Mind; Core p. 208)<br /> Cleanse the Body (Life; 1; Stamina + Medicine + Life; Core p.180)<br /> <br /> <b><u>Nimbus</u></b><br /> <br /> <i>Weak or Uncloaked to Sleepers</i> - There's a hint of invigoration in the immediate surroundings. Colors are a bit more vibrant, light shines a bit brighter, blood pumps a bit quicker.<br /> <br /> <i>Strong or Uncloaked to Mages</i> - The hint becomes a full-on rush, everything seems to take on a life of its own as their Fallen skin begins to crack. In the distance, a voice can be heard.<br /> <br /> <i>Powerful</i> - The cracks widen with thin beams of Supernal light breaking through. The distant voice becomes a choir singing High Speech, as if complimenting an epic scene.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Character Biography</u></b><br /> <br /> <i>Asleep</i> - He was always that problem kid at school, the one you'd swore would end up in jail after graduation (assuming he would graduate, that is). Whether it was beating up kids or sticking it to the Man (be them teachers or otherwise), it seemed he spent more time in the office than in the classroom. It wasn't that he had a problem with authority, he always showed respect and discipline to his martial arts trainer, he just had a problem with bullshit.<br /> <br /> Even as a Sleeper, he could always see past a bit of the Lie. Probably because he enjoyed mythology so much. The tall tales and epic exploits spoke to him in ways people either didn't know how, didn't want to, or perhaps were afraid to. It was fiction on the surface, but truth rang underneath, so long as one was willing to listen. And that frustrated him to no end...<br /> <br /> <i>Awakened</i> - Shortly after Awakening he moved to Boston and joined the Adamantine Arrow there. Since then, he's rapidly progressed in magic, if a little too much (the Awakened world has its fair share of bullshit, and since he tends to get violent in response, well...). Every night, he dreams of a certain Rune. What this Rune is and what it means is a one of the many Mysteries he'll have to chase.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Equipment</u></b><br /> Order Tool - Bo Staff (Damage 2B; Size 4N; Durability 1; +1 Defense in melee combat; Armory p. 32)<br /> Forces Tool - Magnetic Gloves (<a href=\"http://toolmonger.com/2007/12/13/hot-or-not-silverback-magnetic-glove/\" target=\"_blank\">http://toolmonger.com/2007/12/13/hot...agnetic-glove/</a>)<br /> Sports Car (Durability 2; Size 10; Structure 12; Acceleration 15; Safe Speed 103 [70 mph], Maximum Speed 235 [160 mph], Handling 4)<br /> <br /> <b><u>Experience</u></b><br /> Unspent: 0<br /> Spent: 10<br /> <br /> <b>-Optional Details-</b><br /> <u>Age:</u> 19<br /> <u>Gender:</u> Male<br /> <u>Ethnicity:</u> Probably mixed, given his tan skin tone<br /> <u>Nationality:</u> American<br /> <u>Hair Color:</u> Grey<br /> <u>Eye Color:</u> Brown<br /> <u>Sexuality:</u> None of my business<br /> <u>Spirituality:</u> The Monomyth if that counts<br /> <br /> ------------------------------<br /> <br /> Get up, morning ritual, go to school, try to learn as best you can, beat up those same assholes again, blah blah blah. Rinse and repeat. Every. Single. Damn. Day. And after 12 years of this drivel? Just work from here on out now. It's the same dance, just a slightly different tune.<br /> <br /> It felt like Death. He always hated Death, hates it even now. Since when was stagnation ever necessary in the universe anyways?<br /> <br /> He couldn't just fade away on some deathbed. There had to be more to life than this. They may have been fairy tales, but there was truth to the various myths he enjoyed. The heroic journey, it was real, it had to be! The devil was in finding it. That's when she showed up.<br /> <br /> &quot;In order to escape, you have to risk everything,&quot; she said. While she looked somewhere in her thirties, it seemed as though she contained the wisdom of sages beyond the years of mortals.<br /> <br /> He immediately understood what that meant, he knew what needed to be done, but he just didn't know how to go about it. It was like a riddle he knew the answer to, but couldn't find the words to explain it. He racked his brain, trying to figure it out. And he had to do it quick because it was only a few days until graduation, a few days of freedom. Once those passed, he'd be stuffed right back in the machine and that woman would leave. He didn't know how he knew, but he knew.<br /> <br /> In order to escape, you have to risk everything.<br /> <br /> &quot;But how do I risk everything? Where do I go? Where do I look?&quot; he asked her, giving in. He didn't want to resort to calling for help. It was one of those things where you had to figure it out yourself, wasn't it? Asking was cheating, right? But he had no choice, he was simply out of time.<br /> <br /> She let out a slight chuckle. &quot;I was wondering when you were going to ask that.&quot;<br /> <br /> The walls flew away in fright, revealing a landscape of dreams and stars. Truth rang like bells, wisdom performing a harmony unmatched by any human composer. The birthplace of myth. High atop a distant Watchtower shone the light of a golden key. That was the Call, now to answer it.<br /> <br /> Archetypes sprang forth to challenge him. They were the Trials. He defeated them, every victory pouring enlightenment beyond his wildest dreams into him, making every trial easier than the last. He was on a roll, he was going to reach that Watchtower in no time. This is what he wanted after all. And now that he has the opportunity, he wasn't going to let it go.<br /> <br /> Overcoming the last trial, he entered the Watchtower with gleeful anticipation. His expectation of wondrous grandeur was met with painful reality. He wished for a way out of the machine, and a way out this Watchtower would give. But the world he would enter was filled with shadows and secrets, terrible truths and dark paths. And he could never go back once he entered. The Cave.<br /> <br /> His horrifying realization twisted itself into a dragon, and he ran. Ran away to whence he came, trying to escape the corrupting breaths behind him. It wasn't worth it. Nothing was worth this world of darkness. The machine may be boring, but at least one could be sane in there. This new world threatened insanity as the least of its punishments. Only a madman would ever choose to go there.<br /> <br /> He saw the machine in sight, and that's when he stopped. Why? Why wouldn't his legs move? It was only a few steps now, he was right there. He couldn't afford to be in this other world. The dragon approached, each step shaking the ground. Just a few more steps, but something in him just wouldn't budge. The dragon was right behind him, inhaling a lungful.<br /> <br /> In order to escape, you have to risk everything.<br /> <br /> The fire of his soul lit, and he let out a defiant roar against the dragon's breath. This world he knows may be filled with darkness, but that doesn't mean he has to take it lying down. In fact, he owed the world not to take it lying down. It was his duty to conquer this darkness like he did with the dragon, to shine as a hero. Dragons may exist, but they can be killed. He carved his name into the dragon, marking his first victory. Everything faded back into mundane reality, the woman wearing a smirk.<br /> <br /> &quot;That was the Threshold Guardian,&quot; she explained, &quot;For the rest, you're going to have to come with me.&quot;<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Who is that woman in the prelude? She's one of the Awakening Gambit Legacy (Adamantine Arrow p. 161). Past that, I'll let the ST decide. Consider it an NPC to populate the world.<br /> <br /> Also, it's important to note that while Phoenix does indeed meet the requirements of the Tamers of Fire Legacy, he's not actually a part of it yet. The Rune he sees in his dreams is that of the Legacy, but he needs to figure that out first. Then he needs to find a master and be inducted. The reason? The mystery and induction'll be a rich first step into the chronicle and hella fun to play!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","user":"crapcarp","date":". 02-01-2015, 01:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T15:30:30-08:00","id":387680,"title":"","content":"We are just full of Mind mages!<br /> <br /> EDIT: And Life mages.<br /> EDIT2: Holy magicaly specialized cabal Batman!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2347,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","user":"Mahasamatman","date":". 01-31-2015, 06:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","name":"Mahasamatman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2347_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T16:54:32-08:00","id":387792,"title":"","content":"Crapcarp, this is an excellent character submission! A well written Bio and Prelude, and all your mechanical ducks in a row as well. Exactly the kind of thing I'm looking for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","name":"Techpriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T01:05:37-08:00","id":388125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Techpriest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/383264-recruiting-mage-the-awakening-anthology-of-power-play-by-post?p=387792#post387792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Crapcarp, this is an excellent character submission! A well written Bio and Prelude, and all your mechanical ducks in a row as well. Exactly the kind of thing I'm looking for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, I do try. By the way, I've made a few changes. Nothing major, mostly the rotes and stats for a vehicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T20:17:28-08:00","id":389348,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Sorry about the full novel that I almost went for here, but I thought this would be a fun game to jump into. I haven't made a lot of Mage characters for the nWoD as of yet (more of an Ascension person myself), but I'm not going to learn if I'm too stubborn to try new things.<br /> <br /> This is obviously first draft, so I apologize for any glaring errors or egregious typos that are out of place...I think I've cleaned most of them up, but a few may have snuck underneath my radar as I went. Happy to discuss anything else via PM or here, as it's a learning experience either way...<br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">C</