y one to three days. Obviously life causes these things to fluctuate, but once a week is far too slow for the amount of material I've prepared.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","name":"Techpriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T09:51:44-08:00","id":391571,"title":"","content":"So at least twice a week? The rules for character creation are pure vanilla 1st ed. Mage, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T10:12:02-08:00","id":391598,"title":"","content":"At minimum. Yes, original Mage:The Awakening rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","name":"Techpriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T11:52:34-08:00","id":391679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Techpriest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/383264-recruiting-mage-the-awakening-anthology-of-power-play-by-post?p=391523#post391523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi Thorbes. I am still recruiting, so by all means submit a character. And yes, we'll be playing in the Play By Post section of these forums.</div> </div> </div> </div>When are you planning to start the game? Rough estimate would do fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","name":"Mahasamatman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2347_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T12:15:38-08:00","id":391736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Techpriest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/383264-recruiting-mage-the-awakening-anthology-of-power-play-by-post?p=391457#post391457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way NoiseConspiracy, your choice of Cryptography as a specialty works out beautifully for the first story!</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that is perfect. As I said before, I'm aping on the explorer type, so someone searching for ancient mystic artifacts probably has to work their way through more than one puzzle to get there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4859-noiseconspiracy","name":"NoiseConspiracy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4859_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T12:26:54-08:00","id":391747,"title":"","content":"Alright everyone, time for some preliminaries.<br /> <br /> Crapcarp and NoiseConspiracy are officially invited to join the game. Crapcarp I haven't heard from you in the private messages so please let me know that you're still around. While I'm waiting for another submission that I feel fits, I'll go ahead and create the OOC thread. There our players can feel free to discuss the Cabal itself (The name, symbolic theme, and such) and anything else they'd like to talk about.<br /> <br /> Mahasamatman, AngryIceCream, I feel that your styles do not fit well with my own. I appreciate your interest in the game, and the work you put into your characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4803-techpriest","name":"Techpriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T17:52:21-08:00","id":392085,"title":"","content":"Dr. Marvin Bates (otherwise known as Bardo) is ready for inspection. The &quot;Prelude&quot; is actually a little scene of his research and early activities as a mage, rather than the tale of his awakening, that I folded in the Biography part. Hope you like it.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Player:</b> Thorbes<br /> <b>Chronicle:</b> Anthology of Power<br /> <br /> <b>Path:</b> Moros<br /> <b>Order:</b> Free Council<br /> <b>Cabal: </b><br /> <br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Prudence<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Pride<br /> <b>Concept:</b> Left-Handed Doctor<br /> <br /> <b><u>Advantages:</u></b><br /> Health: 7<br /> Willpower: 6<br /> Defense: 2<br /> Initiative: 5<br /> Speed: 9<br /> <br /> Gnosis: 2 (3 Merit dots invested to raise it from 1)<br /> Wisdom: 5 (Reduced due to the hubristic nature of his research. The extra 10xp are spent in 3 1-dot Merits and in buying the second dot of another)*<br /> Mana: 5/11 (2/turn)<br /> <br /> <b><u>Attributes</u> </b><br /> Intelligence: 4<br /> Wits: 2<br /> Resolve: 2<br /> <br /> Strength: 1<br /> Dexterity: 3<br /> Stamina: 2<br /> <br /> Presence: 2<br /> Manipulation: 2<br /> Composure: 4 (free dot from Path)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Skills</u></b><br /> Academics: 1<br /> Computer:<br /> Crafts:<br /> Investigation: 1<br /> Medicine: 4 (Surgery)<br /> Occult: 2 (the Soul)<br /> Politics: 1<br /> Science: 2 (Drugs)<br /> <br /> Athletics:<br /> Brawl:<br /> Drive: 1<br /> Firearms:<br /> Larceny: 1<br /> Stealth: 1<br /> Survival:<br /> Weaponry: 1<br /> <br /> Animal Ken:<br /> Empathy: 1<br /> Expression: 2<br /> Intimidation:<br /> Persuasion: 1<br /> Socialize: 1<br /> Streetwise:<br /> Subterfuge: 2<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Merits</u></b><br /> <br /> Resources: 3 (from his profitable job as a surgeon) [WoD: p.115]<br /> Status (Doctor): 2 (more or less informal status due to his skill)* [WoD: p.116]<br /> Library: 1 (the Soul)* [M:tA: p.85]<br /> Sanctum: 1 (small laboratory)* [M:tA: p.86]<br /> Hallow: 1 (inside the Sanctum, an small washing pile with a resonance of &quot;Cleansing&quot;)* [M.tA: p.83]<br /> High Speech: 1 (Free) [M:tA: p.84]<br /> <br /> <b><u>Arcana</u>:</b> Death 2, Life 2, Matter 2<br /> <br /> <b><u>Rotes</u></b><br /> Forensic Gaze (Death 1; M:tA: p.134)<br /> Soul Marks (Death 1; M:tA: p.135)<br /> Cleanse the Body (Life 1; M:tA: p.180)<br /> Pulse of the Living World (Life 1; M:tA: p.181)<br /> Transmute Water (Matter 2; M:tA: p.197)<br /> <br /> <b><u>Nimbus</u></b><br /> <br /> &quot;Aseptic&quot;: everything turns artificially quiet and clean and the smell of disinfectant permeates the ambience.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Character Biography</u></b><br /> <br /> Born the only son of a traditional bostonian couple that had suffered a couple of abortions, Marvin didn't seem long for this world. Sickly and weak since birth, the child managed to survive the first day of his life against all odds. Then he lived for a week. Then a month. Whether it was little Marvin's determination, the obsesive love of his parents, or something stranger still, the fact is that Marvin succeeded where his stillborn brothers couldn't and managed to grow up to became a child, then a teenager and finally a young adult that was the pride of his parents.<br /> <br /> Although his health was always precarious at best, or maybe as sort of strange compesation of nature, Marvin demonstrated from an early age a vivacious ingenuity and a sharp intellect. Good natured, he decided to use his prodigious faculties to help those like him and so, with the blessing of his parents, he studied to became a doctor. His analitical mind and strong memory served him well and he graduated as the first of his promotion.<br /> <br /> Now Marvin is growing old, his parents died not a couple of years ago and he visits their tomb and that of his stillborn brothers every week. Married to one of his younger colleages and co-workers at the hospital (working in the maternity wing) they still have no child of their own. On one hand the job consumes a lot of time from both of them, and Marvin secretely fears that he may be incapable of siring healthy children as happened to his parents. He doesn't want to visit more small tombs the weekends.<br /> <br /> The Awakening of Dr. Marvin Bates was at once more and less traumatic than most. He was beside the bed where their parents were dying of old age in his own hospital when, maybe due to the emotional overload, things started to get strange. He could felt how with each breath his parents were less and less alive, while nearby in the maternity ward the life was flourishing. As a certain undefinable spark was obviously getting extinguished in his parents, a new light grew stronger by the second in the newborns. Marvin finally awoke when he left the room where his parents laid dead to look for his wife to give her the news, only to saw the unmistakable gaze of his parents coming from a couple of recently born twins.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Equipment</u></b><br /> <br /> Comfy appartement. Good german car. Extensive medical library.<br /> Death Tool: consecrated ashes from a cremated body<br /> Life Tool: his own freshly spilt blood.<br /> Matter Tool(s): Salt, mercury and sulfur.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Experience</u></b><br /> Unspent: 0<br /> Spent: 10<br /> <br /> <b>-Optional Details-</b><br /> <br /> <b>Age: </b>Early forties<br /> <b>Gender: </b>Male<br /> <b>Ethnicity: </b>American of british origin<br /> <b>Nationality: </b>American<br /> <b>Hair Color: </b>Salt and pepper with still mostly black hair, very open forehead. Invariably clean shaven.<br /> <b>Eye Color: </b>Blue-gray<br /> <b>Sexuality:</b> Heterosexual<br /> <b>Spirituality:</b> Marvin believes in reincarnation, specifically in the greek concept of Metempsycosis (also known as Transmigration). He thinks it is his duty to discover the proccess now that he's been given the tools to do so.<br /> <br /> ------------------------------<br /> <b>Prelude</b>:<br /> <br /> Marvin-no, not Marvin, he corrected himself- <i>Bardo</i> looked at the dying man in front of him. Even without aid of any kind of magic it was painfully clear he had no much time left, so Bardo had to work quickly. Fortunately for him the situation had been carefully planned beforehand, so he just needed to follow the protocol.<br /> <br /> He pressed his right thumb against the thin edge of his scalpel, making a tiny cut. He anoited his right eyelid with the blood, the Eye of Life. Then he took a pinch of rock salt from one of the many pockets of his coat and did the same to his left eyelid, the Eye of Matter. Finally, he smeared both his index fingers in some of the ashes he had taken from the morgue's incinerator and draw a crude image of an open eye in his clear forehead, the Eye of Death.<br /> <br /> He activated the timer from his watch. Then he waited.<br /> <br /> Under the mystical triunvirate of his vision, the patterns of the body before him-for it had stoped being a person to Bardo's mind for some minutes now-started to shift balance. There was the Matter of its clothes, and the ever-warring Life and Death patterns that composed his being. The ponderous resonance of that Matter proved too distracting from the subtleties of the soul energy that was being released from the flesh of his subject of investigation. Bardo took a quick mental note to undress the subjects in the future.<br /> <br /> Under the clinical scrutiny of the mage, the Life and Death resonances started to deplete and grow in similar yet inverse proportion, as if the body were a glass filled to the brim with oil and now they were pouring water. It was a matter of minutes before the last strand of Life was about to dissapear. Bardo consulted his watch and made quick note of the time.<br /> <br /> This was always the most difficult part. He took more ashes and covered his hands in them, like how he washed before a procedure. Breathing heavily on them, he prepared, one hand firmly extended over the soon-to-be-corpse, another holding tight the container.<br /> <br /> It was a brief moment that lasted and eternity, an eon in the span of a second. The body's resonance finally collapsed under the weight of Death and the soul was freed. The body became quickly indistinguishable from the clothes that covered it, a mass of Death-tainted Matter. Bardo, true to his adpted name, lived for this intermediate moments. His expert hand seizing the fleeting animus and storing in the container in a single, fluid movement.<br /> <br /> Bardo carefully, almost lovingly, put the soul jar next to the others. He consulted his watch again. It was getting late.<br /> <br /> He made a self-apointment to analize its new especimen tomorrow. He was still only a theory, but he was sure the proccess could be somehow inverted, turning regular Matter into a living being by virtue of a soul. It was just a question of finding how the process by wich souls were originally &quot;anchored&quot; to the body actually worked. He was almost sure it happened at some undefinable moment between conception and birth. With luck, he would find more soon. His wife-no, he corrected himself again-<i>Marvin's</i> wife, had comented she had some new patients at different stages of pregnacy, all of them-he hoped-early enough to be relevant to his research.<br /> <br /> Bardo moved the inert body to the huge tub and covered it with water. He traced an inverted triangle in front of him, the alchemical symbol of water, and the liquid change at once reacting to his will. The acid devoured most of the soft tissue and fabrics in short order, by this time next morning not even the bones would remain.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 02-04-2015, 05:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T18:23:33-08:00","id":392102,"title":"","content":"This is an excellent submission Thorbes. I really enjoyed that Prelude!, very Gothic!<br /> <br /> I realize this is not strictly against the rules, but I'd like to ask that you not have more than one Attribute at 1. I would have said this in the opening post, but its a fairly common limitation and I wasn't expecting it. Other than that personal caveat, I'd like to officially welcome you to the game. That gives us our three players. I'll update the original post to explain that we're full.<br /> <br /> I've already created the OOC Thread here:<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/391814-ooc-mage-the-awakening-anthology-of-power\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/g...ology-of-power</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""